ogesterone balance during the luteal phase, and improve menstrual cycle regularity. Additionally, flaxseed may help manage weight swings and reduce cravings and appetite fluctuations associated with hormonal changes. The high fiber content in flaxseed promotes satiety, potentially leading to decreased calorie intake and better appetite control.*<br> <br><i>Helps: Supports hormonal balance, aids in managing occasional bloating, promotes menstrual cycle comfort, and may assist in weight management by reducing cravings and appetite fluctuations.*<br></i><br><br><strong>Ginger Root Extract<br></strong><br>Ginger contains bioactive compounds like gingerols and shogaols that inhibit prostaglandin synthesis via COX and LOX pathways. This anti-inflammatory action helps reduce menstrual cramps and digestive discomfort.<br> <br><i>Helps: Aids in managing occasional cramps, supports digestive wellness, and promotes natural cycle comfort.*<br></i><br><br><strong>Aniseed Extract<br></strong><br>Aniseed has carminative and antispasmodic properties that relax gastrointestinal muscles, alleviating bloating, cramps, and other digestive discomforts.<br><br><i>Helps: Promotes soothing comfort during cyces, supports digestion, and eases occasional tension.*<br></i><br><br><strong>Turmeric Root Extract<br></strong><br>Curcumin in turmeric has anti-inflammatory properties that help reduce menstrual discomfort by targeting inflammatory pathways and promoting bile production to alleviate bloating.*<br><br><i>Helps: Promotes comfort during cycles, supports natural inflammation balance, and aids in managing bloating.*</i></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="99b70e9c-12b5-4fd9-85bb-ab3217bee4c9" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1fvxmj1" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="ee1c6adf-a54a-44b0-8e1b-d67b98e0f3c6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rair2:" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" tabi